{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 44, :comments ["<b>The sons of Asher.</b> Defective here — missing ישוה; therefore Rashi explained, regarding 'to the ears I say,' that this is the clan of Etsbon, for if it were so (a certain reading), that the clan of Etsbon had fallen, then eight clans would have fallen: five to Binyamin, and Ehud, and Etsbon, and Yishvah." "<b>לבריעה.</b> The sons of Beriah were divided into three clans: one named after him, and two after Hever and Malkiel."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:50.349762504Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}